{"id": "biz-4", "headline": "Nebraska Medicaid work rules: paperwork drives coverage loss", "source": "KFF Health News", "url": "https://kffhealthnews.org/health-care-costs/medicaid-work-requirements-new-rules-coverage-dropped-nebraska-rollout/", "published": "2026-11-25", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Nebraska started Medicaid work requirements eight months before the 2025 federal budget law required them, and its early rollout is being watched as a preview for the rest of the country. Analysts had feared people would lose coverage because of system glitches. KFF Health News reports that enrollees are losing coverage because of paperwork, not because they are not working. More than three dozen other states are due to follow in 2027. On November 13 the Trump administration let states take until July 2027, instead of January, to begin dropping people who do not comply. States have until December 11 to decide whether to proceed on January 1. Congressional Democrats, including Sen.", "Ron Wyden, said the delay confirmed their warnings about red tape. Source: KFF Health News."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110010100101011110100001011101111111", "10000010100010011010110000111110001000001", "10111010000010111010011000111011101011101", "10111010101110000011000111110101101011101", "10111010011000111010010100001011101011101", "10000010110001000110100000010000101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000000110001001111110110000100000000", "11111011100001100101001111110100010101010", "01110100100001000111100110001001111111011", "01001010010001111100011000110010001000010", "01111000111111000110111000010000010111001", "11110010010100101000001011001101000001110", "00001001110010010011001101001011111111101", "11111011101000111010001000110100000111000", "01100101110010110000111110010001111111010", "00001111000011110100001011110100000000100", "01110101100100101011111101101001111110001", "11010111011000010010100010111100000100000", "111011000000001000001101